Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER
Task name: /root
Sender: /root/review_error_handling
Payload:
Found three concrete `error_handling_missing` candidates:

1. `packages/twyne-tools/src/client.ts:68` — severity 3, confidence 0.99

```ts
  async request<T>(request: IntegrationRequest, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<T> {
    let response: Response;
    try {
      response = await this.fetchImpl(this.endpoint, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
          authorization: `Bearer ${this.accessToken}`,
          "content-type": "application/json",
          accept: "application/json",
          "user-agent": "@twyne/tools",
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(request),
        signal,
      });
```

The client has no default request timeout, and every CLI/MCP call omits `signal`. A stalled endpoint can therefore leave a CLI command or MCP tool call pending for several minutes or indefinitely. Add a bounded internal timeout, merged with any caller signal, and translate timeout/body-read failures into `TwyneApiError`.

2. `packages/twyne-tools/src/archive.ts:209` — severity 3, confidence 0.95

```ts
export async function importSources(client: TwyneClient, sources: ImportSource[]): Promise<ImportSummary> {
  const imported: Folio[] = [];
  const warnings: string[] = [];
  let citationsSaved = 0;
  for (const source of sources) {
    const parsed = parseImportSource(source);
    for (const bundle of parsed.folios) {
      const folio = await client.putFolio({
        folio: bundle.folio,
        ...(bundle.html !== undefined ? { html: bundle.html } : {}),
        ...(bundle.brief !== undefined ? { brief: bundle.brief } : {}),
      });
      imported.push(folio);
      if (bundle.citations?.length && folio.id) {
        const result = await client.putCitations(folio.id, bundle.citations as CitationEntry[]);
        citationsSaved += result.saved;
      }
```

Bulk import mutates remote state incrementally without rollback, compensation, or partial-result reporting. A malformed later source, network failure, or citation failure rejects the whole call after earlier folios were saved; the CLI/MCP returns only an error and loses the successfully imported IDs. Retrying ID-less Markdown/HTML/text imports duplicates those earlier folios. Pre-validate all sources and either use an atomic server-side operation or return explicit per-item successes/failures.

3. `src/utils/standard-site.ts:252` — severity 3, confidence 0.96

```ts
    const created = await agent.com.atproto.repo.createRecord({
      repo: did,
      collection: STANDARD_SITE_DOCUMENT_COLLECTION,
      record: documentRecord({
        folio,
        html,
        brief,
        publicationUri: publication.uri,
        publishedAt,
        updatedAt: now,
      }),
    });
    uri = created.data.uri;
    rkey = rkeyFromUri(uri, STANDARD_SITE_DOCUMENT_COLLECTION);
    const updated = await agent.com.atproto.repo.putRecord({
      repo: did,
      collection: STANDARD_SITE_DOCUMENT_COLLECTION,
      rkey,
      record: documentRecord({
        folio,
        html,
        brief,
        publicationUri: publication.uri,
        path: standardSiteDocumentPath(rkey),
        publishedAt,
        updatedAt: now,
      }),
    });
```

First publication performs two external writes but handles no partial failure. If `createRecord` succeeds and `putRecord` fails, the PDS retains an incomplete document while local metadata is never saved. Retrying creates another record, leaving an orphan. Generate a stable rkey before writing when possible, or catch the second failure and delete/persist the created record so retry is idempotent.

